The logic is unchanged. Two small changes are aimed at speed, though I haven't measured the gain:

- The common path, a field whose own type is already set, is marked as likely with `__builtin_expect`. The compiler can then lay it out as a straight fall-through branch.
- `profile` is read once into a local variable, so the profile path does not re-read the member.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const Profile::MSG* const p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```